'''Group A of the 1994 FIFA World Cup''' was one of six groups of four teams competing at the [[1994 FIFA World Cup|1994 World Cup]] in the United States. The first matches were played June 18, 1994, and the final games took place simultaneously on June 26, 1994.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/tournaments/archive/worldcup/usa1994/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131220184449/http://www.fifa.com/tournaments/archive/worldcup/usa1994/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=December 20, 2013|title=1994 FIFA World Cup USA|publisher=fifa.com|accessdate=July 31, 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/94full.html|title=World Cup 1994|website=[[RSSSF]]|accessdate=July 31, 2014}}</ref>

The group consisted of one [[CONCACAF]] team, the host [[United States men's national soccer team|United States]]; two [[UEFA]] teams, [[Switzerland national football team|Switzerland]] and [[Romania national football team|Romania]]; and one [[CONMEBOL]] team, [[Colombia national football team|Colombia]]. Romania won the group, Switzerland finished second and also the United States advanced to the knockout stage as one of the best third-placed teams. Colombia finished last with only three points.

